---
// ProseCodeCopy (D-064, D-112): a "Copy code" button on every `pre` inside prose (`.ocx-prose`,
// `.sl-markdown-content`, `.vp-doc`), for content that is plain HTML: a mirrored README, docs
// rendered without Expressive Code. Place it once on a page that has prose: its script loads wherever
// it renders, so not in a layout every page shares. It renders no markup. The button is inserted by
// script (prose-code-copy.mjs); the first click loads the clipboard and toast code, copies the block's
// code and asks the page toaster for "Copied — code block". Starlight's Expressive Code frames are skipped: they have their own.
import './prose-code-copy.css';
---

<script>
  import { enhanceProseCode } from './prose-code-copy.mjs';
  enhanceProseCode(document);
</script>
